Title: The Impact of the New 59Fe Decay Rates on 60Fe and 26Al Nucleosynthesis in Massive Stars
Authors: Tan B., Xin W., Jiang R., Zhao G., and Takahashi K.
Table: 26Al and 60Fe yields
================================================================================
Byte-by-byte Description of file: table.dat
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Bytes Format Units  Label     Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1- 2  A2      ---    Fe59_decay_rate Decay rate of 59Fe, DR=Default Rate (LMP,
                                    2001); NR=New Rate (Gao et al., 2021)
 4- 5  I2     solMass M_ini           [14/80] Initial mass of the star
 7-14  E8.3   solMass M_tot_26Al      [0.0/0.01] Total ejected mass of 26Al
16-23  E8.3   solMass M_wind_26Al     [0.0/0.01] Ejected mass of 26Al from
                                    stellar winds
25-32  E8.3   solMass M_sh_26Al       [0.0/0.01] The contribution of shell
                                    burning to the total ejected mass of 26Al
34-43  E10.3  solMass M_exp_26Al      [-0.01/0.01] The net contribution of the
                                    supernova explosion to the total ejected
                                    mass of 26Al
45-52  E8.3   solMass M_tot_60Fe      [0.0/0.01] Total ejected mass of 60Fe
54-61  E8.3   solMass M_sh_60Fe       [0.0/0.01] The contribution of shell
                                    burning to the total ejected mass of 60Fe
63-72  E10.3  solMass M_exp_60Fe      [-0.01/0.01] The net contribution of the
                                    supernova explosion to the total ejected
                                    mass of 60Fe
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
